{"bill":{"id":"119-hr-1971","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"1971","title":"Veterans SPORT Act","introducedDate":"2025-03-10","latestActionDate":"2025-03-25","latestActionText":"Forwarded by Subcommittee to Full Committee by Voice Vote.","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","subjects":["Athletes","Health technology, devices, supplies","Outdoor recreation","Veterans' medical care"],"sponsorBioguideId":"M001215","cosponsorBioguideIds":["M001199"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"officialSummary":"Veterans Supporting Prosthetics Opportunities and Recreational Therapy Act or the Veterans SPORT Act This bill includes adaptive prostheses and terminal devices for sports and other recreational activities within the definition of medical services under the laws administered by the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA). Under the bill, these artificial limbs must be furnished as medical services to eligible veterans.","congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1971","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/hr/BILLSTATUS-119hr1971.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:29:52.409Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-hr-1971","plainSummary":"This bill would require the Department of Veterans Affairs to provide adaptive prosthetic limbs and terminal devices designed for sports and recreational activities to eligible veterans. Currently, VA medical services cover standard prosthetics; this legislation would expand that definition to include specialized equipment for athletic and outdoor activities. The change would make these recreational prostheses available as part of standard VA medical care rather than requiring separate approval or funding.","industries":[{"industry":"pharma","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"Medical device manufacturers that produce adaptive prosthetics and terminal devices would see expanded demand through VA procurement."},{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"VA health systems would need to furnish and fit these specialized prosthetic devices as part of their medical services."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"78227abc948a61e9a323f003","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:50:45.696Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoes":"This bill would include adaptive prostheses and terminal devices for sports and other recreational activities within the definition of medical services under the laws administered by the VA.","whoItTouches":"Veterans and their families.","everydayEffect":"If it passed, the change would show up in what the VA does for you. Nothing has changed yet. Most bills never become law.","confidence":"crs-summary","source":"Reworded from the official summary. Staff at the Congressional Research Service wrote that summary. It is public domain, and the full text of it is further down this page.","titleInPlainWords":null},"overlaps":[{"billId":"119-hr-1971","bioguideId":"M001215","cycle":2026,"score":0.030756200935957156,"matches":[{"industry":"health-providers","donorAmount":207500,"donorShare":0.05042921005471346,"billConfidence":0.5,"contribution":0.01867748520544943},{"industry":"pharma","donorAmount":78935.35,"donorShare":0.019183842630806393,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.012078715730507728}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.6907052625155475},"member":{"name":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks","chamber":"House","state":"IA","district":"1","imageUrl":"data/portraits/M001215.jpg","role":"Sponsor"},"donorProfile":{"bioguideId":"M001215","cycle":2026,"totalItemized":4114678.77,"byIndustry":[{"industry":"health-providers","amount":207500,"share":0.05042921005471346,"contributionCount":84},{"industry":"party-leadership","amoun